==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|hinn|}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*jainaz}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|yon||that, that one over there}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈhɪnː/}}
* {{rhymes|is|ɪnː}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun|feminine|hin|neuter|hitt}}

# {{lb|is|demonstrative}} [[other]], the other, the other one, the [[next]]; [[that]] (in conjunction with {{m|is|þessi||this, that}})
#* Luke 6:29 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke%206:29&version=NIV English], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke%206:29&version=ICELAND Icelandic])
#*: ''Slái þig einhver á kinnina, skaltu og bjóða '''hina''', og taki einhver yfirhöfn þína, skaltu ekki varna honum að taka kyrtilinn líka.''
#*:: If someone strikes you on one cheek, turn to him the '''other''' also. If someone takes your cloak, do not stop him from taking your tunic.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-pron-hinn}}

===Article===
{{head|is|article|feminine|hin|neuter|hið}}

# [[the]] (definite article)
#* Genesis 1:31 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20b%C3%B3k%20M%C3%B3se+1:31&version=ICELAND Icelandic Bible], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20b%C3%B3k%20M%C3%B3se%201:31&version=NIV New International Version])
#*: ''Og Guð leit allt, sem hann hafði gjört, og sjá, það var harla gott. Það varð kveld og það varð morgunn, '''hinn''' sjötti dagur.''
#*:: God saw all that he had made, and it was very good. And there was evening, and there was morning—'''the''' sixth day.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-art-hinn}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|the}} {{l|is|-inn}}, {{l|is|inn}}, {{l|is|enn}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|hið opinbera}}

